IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fpa-dates`
IMPORT `fpa-rules`
IMPORT `fpa-claimant`

-- Family Provision Act 1969 (ACT) -- worked cases for the questions of the family member claiming provision.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names used below`

yes MEANS TRUE
no MEANS FALSE

`1 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2026
`10 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 3 2026
`1 May 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 5 2026
`31 Aug 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 8 2026
`1 Sep 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 9 2026
`10 Sep 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 9 2026
`11 Sep 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 11 9 2026
`20 Sep 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 20 9 2026
`25 Sep 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 25 9 2026
`30 Sep 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 9 2026
`1 Oct 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 10 2026
`15 Dec 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 12 2026
`28 Feb 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2027
`1 Mar 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2027
`30 Mar 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 3 2027
`15 Jun 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 6 2027
`31 Aug 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 8 2027
`29 Feb 2028` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2028

`NOT STARTED` MEANS `the 6 months have not started: no administration of the estate has been granted in the ACT yet`
`IN TIME` MEANS `applied in time`
`STILL IN TIME` MEANS `not yet applied, still in time`
`LATE, EXTEND` MEANS `out of time: you need the Supreme Court to extend the time (s 9 (2)), which it may do whether or not the time has ended`
`LATE, TOO LATE` MEANS `out of time, and no extension can now be asked for: the estate has been lawfully and fully distributed (s 9 (4))`

`HEAD A` MEANS `s 7 (1) (a): a partner of the deceased`
`HEAD B` MEANS `s 7 (1) (b): a person in a domestic relationship with the deceased for 2 or more years continuously`
`HEAD C` MEANS `s 7 (1) (c): a child of the deceased`
`HEAD D` MEANS `s 7 (1) (d): a stepchild of the deceased, maintained by the deceased immediately before death`
`HEAD E` MEANS `s 7 (1) (e): a grandchild of the deceased who meets s 7 (3)`
`HEAD F` MEANS `s 7 (1) (f): a parent of the deceased who meets s 7 (4)`

-- Argument order for s 7 and s 8: domestic partner, spouse or civil partner, years as domestic partner, parent of their
-- child, years in a domestic relationship, child, stepchild, grandchild, parent, maintenance order, maintained, court
-- could order maintenance, linking parent died first, a parent survived, maintained by a parent, left a partner, left a
-- child (and, for s 8, the court is satisfied).

§ `s 7 -- who may apply`

-- A spouse who lived with the deceased: a partner (s 7 (9) (a), (b) (i)).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` yes yes 10 no 10 no no no no no no no no no no no yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7 -- the paragraphs I may apply under` yes yes 10 no 10 no no no no no no no no no no no yes EQUALS LIST `HEAD A`
-- A de facto partner of exactly 2 years: a partner (s 7 (9) (b) (ii), "2 or more years").
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` yes no 2 no 2 no no no no no no no no no no no no EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 1.9 years, no child together: not a partner, and short of the 2 years in s 7 (1) (b): NOTHING (a limit in the list's own wording).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` yes no 1.9 no 1.9 no no no no no no no no no no no no EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7 -- the paragraphs I may apply under` yes no 1.9 no 1.9 no no no no no no no no no no no no EQUALS EMPTY
-- 1 year, but the parent of the deceased's child: a partner (s 7 (9) (b) (iii)).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` yes no 1 yes 1 no no no no no no no no no no no yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A carer in a domestic relationship (not a domestic partner) for exactly 2 years: s 7 (1) (b).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- the paragraphs I may apply under` no no 0 no 2 no no no no no no no no no no no no EQUALS LIST `HEAD B`
-- The same carer at 1.99 years: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 1.99 no no no no no no no no no no no no EQUALS NOTHING
-- A partner with a 5-year domestic relationship comes in under (a) only: (b) excludes a partner.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- the paragraphs I may apply under` yes yes 5 no 5 no no no no no no no no no no no no EQUALS LIST `HEAD A`
-- A spouse who was never a domestic partner (as answered): not a partner under s 7 (9) (a); NOTHING (finding 2).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no yes 0 no 0 no no no no no no no no no no no no EQUALS NOTHING
-- A child.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 0 yes no no no no no no no no no no no EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7 -- the paragraphs I may apply under` no no 0 no 0 yes no no no no no no no no no no no EQUALS LIST `HEAD C`
-- A stepchild not maintained: JUST FALSE (s 7 (2), "not entitled ... unless").
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 0 no yes no no no no no no no no yes no EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A stepchild the deceased was contributing to: JUST TRUE, under (d).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 0 no yes no no no yes no no no no yes no EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7 -- the paragraphs I may apply under` no no 0 no 0 no yes no no no yes no no no no yes no EQUALS LIST `HEAD D`
-- A stepchild with a court maintenance order in force: maintained (s 7 (7) (a)).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 0 no yes no no yes no no no no no yes no EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A stepchild for whom a court could have ordered maintenance: maintained (s 7 (7) (c)).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 0 no yes no no no no yes no no no yes no EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A grandchild whose parent (the deceased's child) died first: s 7 (3) (a).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- the paragraphs I may apply under` no no 0 no 0 no no yes no no no no yes no no no yes EQUALS LIST `HEAD E`
-- A grandchild, a parent alive, not maintained by a parent but maintained by the deceased: s 7 (3) (b).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 0 no no yes no no yes no no yes no no yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same grandchild, but also maintained by a parent: JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 0 no no yes no no yes no no yes yes no yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A grandchild, a parent alive, maintained by no one: JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 0 no no yes no no no no no yes no no yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A parent the deceased maintained: s 7 (4) (a).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- the paragraphs I may apply under` no no 0 no 0 no no no yes no yes no no no no yes yes EQUALS LIST `HEAD F`
-- A parent not maintained; the deceased left no partner and no child: s 7 (4) (b).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 0 no no no yes no no no no no no no no EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A parent not maintained; the deceased left a child: JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 0 no no no yes no no no no no no no yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A parent not maintained; the deceased left a partner: JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 0 no no no yes no no no no no no yes no EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An unmaintained stepchild who was also in a 1-year domestic relationship: the text's no for the stepchild wins over NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 1 no yes no no no no no no no no no no EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A stepchild and grandchild (through a child who died first), maintained: under (d) and (e).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- the paragraphs I may apply under` no no 0 no 0 no yes yes no no yes no yes no no no yes EQUALS LIST `HEAD D`, `HEAD E`
-- None of the listed relatives (a friend, a sibling): NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- may I apply for provision out of the estate` no no 0 no 0 no no no no no no no no no no yes yes EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 8 -- the family provision order`

-- A child, the court satisfied: JUST TRUE.
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can the court order provision for me` no no 0 no 0 yes no no no no no no no no no no no yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A child, the court not satisfied adequate provision is lacking: JUST FALSE ("shall only make an order ... if satisfied").
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can the court order provision for me` no no 0 no 0 yes no no no no no no no no no no no no EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An unmaintained stepchild, even with the court satisfied: JUST FALSE (s 7 (2)).
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can the court order provision for me` no no 0 no 0 no yes no no no no no no no no no no yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A sibling, the court satisfied: NOTHING (not in s 7 (1)).
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can the court order provision for me` no no 0 no 0 no no no no no no no no no no no no yes EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 9 -- the time for applying`

-- The last day: same day 6 months on; a shorter month gives its last day; a leap February; across a year end.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the last day to apply` `10 Mar 2026` EQUALS `10 Sep 2026`
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the last day to apply` `31 Aug 2026` EQUALS `28 Feb 2027`
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the last day to apply` `31 Aug 2027` EQUALS `29 Feb 2028`
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the last day to apply` `30 Sep 2026` EQUALS `30 Mar 2027`
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the last day to apply` `15 Dec 2026` EQUALS `15 Jun 2027`

-- Argument order: granted, the grant, applied, applied on, today, extended, extended to, fully distributed.
-- No grant yet.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` no `10 Mar 2026` no `10 Mar 2026` `1 May 2026` no `10 Mar 2026` no EQUALS `NOT STARTED`
-- Filed on the last day (10 September 2026): in time.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` yes `10 Mar 2026` yes `10 Sep 2026` `1 Oct 2026` no `10 Mar 2026` no EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- Filed the day after: out of time, an extension may be asked for.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` yes `10 Mar 2026` yes `11 Sep 2026` `1 Oct 2026` no `10 Mar 2026` no EQUALS `LATE, EXTEND`
-- Filed the day after, the estate fully distributed: too late for an extension.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` yes `10 Mar 2026` yes `11 Sep 2026` `1 Oct 2026` no `10 Mar 2026` yes EQUALS `LATE, TOO LATE`
-- Filed on the day of the grant: in time.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` yes `10 Mar 2026` yes `10 Mar 2026` `1 May 2026` no `10 Mar 2026` no EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- Filed before the grant: counted as day 0, in time (fork F4).
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` yes `10 Mar 2026` yes `1 Mar 2026` `1 May 2026` no `10 Mar 2026` no EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- Not yet filed, today is the last day: still in time.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` yes `10 Mar 2026` no `10 Mar 2026` `10 Sep 2026` no `10 Mar 2026` no EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
-- Not yet filed, today is the day after: out of time.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` yes `10 Mar 2026` no `10 Mar 2026` `11 Sep 2026` no `10 Mar 2026` no EQUALS `LATE, EXTEND`
-- Time extended to 30 September; filed 25 September: in time.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` yes `10 Mar 2026` yes `25 Sep 2026` `1 Oct 2026` yes `30 Sep 2026` no EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- Time extended to 30 September; filed on it: in time; filed 1 October: out of time.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` yes `10 Mar 2026` yes `30 Sep 2026` `1 Oct 2026` yes `30 Sep 2026` no EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` yes `10 Mar 2026` yes `1 Oct 2026` `1 Oct 2026` yes `30 Sep 2026` no EQUALS `LATE, EXTEND`
-- Time extended to 30 September; not filed, today 20 September: still in time.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` yes `10 Mar 2026` no `10 Mar 2026` `20 Sep 2026` yes `30 Sep 2026` no EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
-- An "extension" to a day before the 6 months end does not shorten them: filed 10 September still in time.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- am I in time to apply` yes `10 Mar 2026` yes `10 Sep 2026` `1 Oct 2026` yes `1 Sep 2026` no EQUALS `IN TIME`

-- s 9 (4): more time.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- can I still ask for more time` no EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9 -- can I still ask for more time` yes EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `ss 9A, 10 -- after applying, and changing an order`

#ASSERT `s 10 -- must I serve the administrators` yes
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 10 -- must I serve the administrators` no))

#ASSERT `s 9A (3) -- can my provision be increased` yes yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9A (3) -- can my provision be increased` yes no EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9A (3) -- can my provision be increased` no yes EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 9A (4) -- must I be served with an application to cut my provision` yes yes
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 9A (4) -- must I be served with an application to cut my provision` yes no))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 9A (4) -- must I be served with an application to cut my provision` no yes))

§ `ss 13, 20, 21 -- where the provision can come from`

-- Argument order for s 13: applied, a power exercised by will, the rest is not enough, special circumstances.
#ASSERT `s 13 -- can my provision come from appointed property` yes yes yes no EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13 -- can my provision come from appointed property` yes yes no yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13 -- can my provision come from appointed property` yes yes no no EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13 -- can my provision come from appointed property` yes no yes yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13 -- can my provision come from appointed property` no yes yes yes EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Argument order for s 20: made for a dependant, the grant, distributed on, notice first, vested.
-- Grant 10 March 2026; the 6 months end 10 September 2026.
-- Made for a dependant's maintenance: barred.
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can distributed property be used for my provision` yes `10 Mar 2026` `1 May 2026` yes no EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Distributed 11 September (more than 6 months), no notice, vested: barred.
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can distributed property be used for my provision` no `10 Mar 2026` `11 Sep 2026` no yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Distributed on 10 September (not more than 6 months): not barred.
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can distributed property be used for my provision` no `10 Mar 2026` `10 Sep 2026` no yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Distributed 11 September after notice of the application: not barred.
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can distributed property be used for my provision` no `10 Mar 2026` `11 Sep 2026` yes yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Distributed 11 September, no notice, not yet vested in possession: not barred.
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can distributed property be used for my provision` no `10 Mar 2026` `11 Sep 2026` no no EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Grant 31 August 2026; the 6 months end 28 February 2027: distributed that day not barred, the next day barred.
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can distributed property be used for my provision` no `31 Aug 2026` `28 Feb 2027` no yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20 -- can distributed property be used for my provision` no `31 Aug 2026` `1 Mar 2027` no yes EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Argument order for s 21: as s 20, then s 64 notice given and expired.
-- A s 20 (2) distribution: no action lies.
#ASSERT `s 21 -- can I sue the administrator for distributing` yes `10 Mar 2026` `1 May 2026` yes no no EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21 -- can I sue the administrator for distributing` no `10 Mar 2026` `11 Sep 2026` no yes no EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Distributed 1 May 2026 before notice, after the s 64 notice expired: no action lies.
#ASSERT `s 21 -- can I sue the administrator for distributing` no `10 Mar 2026` `1 May 2026` no yes yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same, but the s 64 time had not expired: the Act is silent.
#ASSERT `s 21 -- can I sue the administrator for distributing` no `10 Mar 2026` `1 May 2026` no yes no EQUALS NOTHING
-- Distributed after notice of the application, the s 64 time expired: the Act is silent.
#ASSERT `s 21 -- can I sue the administrator for distributing` no `10 Mar 2026` `11 Sep 2026` yes yes yes EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 14, 16, 19, 22 -- the order and what follows`

#ASSERT `s 14 -- must I give an undertaking before I am paid` yes yes
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 14 -- must I give an undertaking before I am paid` yes no))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 14 -- must I give an undertaking before I am paid` no yes))

#ASSERT `s 14 -- what I would have to pay back` 10000 5000 yes EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `s 14 -- what I would have to pay back` 10000 5000 no EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `s 14 -- what I would have to pay back` 0 5000 yes EQUALS 5000

#ASSERT `s 16 -- how my order takes effect` no EQUALS `as if it were a codicil to the deceased's will, made immediately before death (s 16 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- how my order takes effect` yes EQUALS `as a modification of the Administration and Probate Act 1929 part 3A (the intestacy rules) for that property (s 16 (2))`

#ASSERT `s 19 -- is my dealing with the provision effective` no EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19 -- is my dealing with the provision effective` yes EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 22 -- can the deceased's statement of reasons be evidence` yes yes yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- can the deceased's statement of reasons be evidence` yes no yes EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22 -- can the deceased's statement of reasons be evidence` no yes yes EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22 -- can the deceased's statement of reasons be evidence` yes yes no EQUALS NOTHING
